          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em local Langlands conjectures
            are certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjectures"} conjectures
            in the context of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Langlands+program"} Langlands program
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Langlands+correspondence"} Langlands correspondence
            concerns
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+fields"} global fields
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+fields"} local fields
          %p
            In the case of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+group"} algebraic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_n
            (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                F-semisimple Weil-Deligne
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
                (see Def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeilDeligneRepresentation"}
                below) of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+group"} Weil group
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+field"} local field
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irrep"} irreducible
                admissible
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi GL
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_n(F)
                (see Def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IrreducibleAndAdmissibleSubgroups"}
                below),
          %p
            generalizing local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class+field+theory"} class field theory
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+groups"} Galois groups
            to non-abelian Galois groups.
          %p
            More generally, it states that for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+field"} local field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reductive+group"} reductive group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
            of irreducible admissible representations of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(F)
            are partitioned into
            %em L-packets
            by the equivalence classes of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-parameters"} L-parameters
          %h2#definitions Definitions:
          %p
            We discuss some of the basic definitions, see also
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Tate77"} Tate 77
          %p Throughout:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+field"} p-adic field
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                denoting its
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/residue+field"} residue field
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reductive+group"} reductive group
          %p
          #IrreducibleAndAdmissibleSubgroups.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representations"} irreducible
                and admissible representations)
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+representation"} linear representation
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(F)
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is called:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irrep"} irreducible
                  if the only
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(F)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+subspaces"} invariant subspaces
